                        "entry_id": "71edbf8c-f074-3ab2-b1eb-13639a3fa8a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "филос. философское идеалистическое направление, признающее разум основой познания и поведения людей, источником и критерием истинности всех жизненных устремлений человека"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ed0af00a-5b86-3f1f-8b36-05e8901adf23",
                        "entry_id": "71edbf8c-f074-3ab2-b1eb-13639a3fa8a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "искусств. авангардистский стиль в архитектуре, характеризующийся лаконичностью форм, строгостью и подчёркнутым функционализмом"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c70e05f1-cf2f-3391-af88-528226a2a9b0",
                        "entry_id": "71edbf8c-f074-3ab2-b1eb-13639a3fa8a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. рассудочное отношение к жизни, рассудочность в поступках"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "01946fbf-1ed1-473d-9f5d-0712dc1845f4",
                        "source_entry_id": "71edbf8c-f074-3ab2-b1eb-13639a3fa8a6",
                        "target_lang_word": "rationalism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rationalism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7813435e-0417-30e5-a628-af6b49a0ac03",
                                        "entry_id": "16fb52fc-2fd6-3218-a92f-a601a39af6a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The theory that the reason is a source of knowledge independent of and superior to sense perception."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "635ac29b-c28f-3986-8ebb-04aee7886d68",
                                        "entry_id": "16fb52fc-2fd6-3218-a92f-a601a39af6a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The theory that knowledge may be derived by deductions from a priori concepts (such as axioms, postulates or earlier deductions)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b8d5bdc-0f01-3412-8431-0c2ccc66e537",
                                        "entry_id": "16fb52fc-2fd6-3218-a92f-a601a39af6a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A view that the fundamental method for problem solving is through reason and experience rather than faith, inspiration, revelation, intuition or authority."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4ada588-8fd9-4113-b321-251848401255",
                                                "sense_id": "0b8d5bdc-0f01-3412-8431-0c2ccc66e537",
                                                "text": "The opinion opposed to mysticism in philosophy is sometimes spoken of as rationalism. Rationalism insists that all our beliefs ought ultimately to find for themselves articulate grounds. Such grounds, for rationalism, must consist of four things: (1) definitely statable abstract principles; (2) definite facts of sensation; (3) definite hypotheses based on such facts; and (4) definite inferences logically drawn."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "10169985-0167-39a6-941a-1710cff993dc",
                                        "entry_id": "16fb52fc-2fd6-3218-a92f-a601a39af6a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Elaboration of theories by use of reason alone without appeal to experience, such as in mathematical systems."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4c22f8a8-302a-4b3e-a3a1-1339e8434499",
                        "source_entry_id": "71edbf8c-f074-3ab2-b1eb-13639a3fa8a6",
                        "target_lang_word": "racionalismo",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "racionalismo",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75962b7d-8a61-31b9-af9e-d16325a38e32",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb173c4-d2a7-3722-be70-72668972429f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sistema de pensamiento que prioriza el papel de la razón en la adquisición del conocimiento, en contraste con el empirismo, que resalta el de la experiencia, sobre todo el sentido de la percepción."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b2772f1-bfad-38c1-b8c0-c3e571b14f82",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb173c4-d2a7-3722-be70-72668972429f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sistema filosófico que dice que las creencias religiosas deben estar fundadas en la razón."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b3c2a8e-ca18-3ab6-b81d-1c870dce4a6a",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb173c4-d2a7-3722-be70-72668972429f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "movimiento surgido tras la Segunda Guerra Mundial en oposición a la imitación de lo antiguo y adopción de un excesivo tecnicismo estandarizador. Se manifiesta en la predilección por las formas geométricas simples, con criterios ortogonales y espacios funcionales."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1dc377d5-5fb9-4229-b666-ffe1f9423a49",
                        "source_entry_id": "71edbf8c-f074-3ab2-b1eb-13639a3fa8a6",
